n-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Villa</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Urioste</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Bofarull</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Mart&#x000ed;nez-Fr&#x000ed;as</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name></person-group>:<article-title>De novo interstitial deletion q16.2q21 on chromosome 6</article-title>.<source>Am J Med Genet</source><year>1995</year>;<volume>55</volume>:<fpage>379</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>383</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7726240</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B9"><label>9.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Holder</surname><given-names>JL</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></name><name><surname>Butte</surname><given-names>NF</given-names></name><name><surname>Zinn</surname><given-names>AR</given-names></name></person-group>:<article-title>Profound obesity associated with a balanced translocation that disrupts the SIM1 gene</article-title>.<source>Hum Mol Genet</source><year>2000</year>;<volume>9</volume>:<fpage>101</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>108</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10587584</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B10"><label>10.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gilhuis</surname><given-names>HJ</given-names></name><name><surname>van Ravenswaaij</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name><name><surname>Hamel</surname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Gabre&#x000eb;ls</surname><given-names>FJ</given-names></name></person-group>:<article-title>Interstitial 6q deletion with a Prader-Willi-like phenotype: a new case and review of the literature</article-title>.<source>Eur J Paediatr Neurol</source><year>2000</year>;<volume>4</volume>:<fpage>39</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>43</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10701104</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B11"><label>11.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Faivre</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Cormier-Daire</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Lapierre</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Colleaux</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Jacquemont</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Genevi&#x000e9;ve</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Saunier</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Munnich</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Turleau</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Romana</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Prieur</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>De Blois</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name><name><surname>Vekemans</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group>:<article-title>Deletion of the SIM1 gene (6q16.2) in a patient with a Prader-Willi-like phenotype</article-title>.<source>J Med Genet</source><year>2002</year>;<volume>39</volume>:<fpage>594</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>596</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12161602</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B12"><label>12.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Varela</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name><name><surname>Sim&#x000f5;es-Sato</surname><given-names>AY</given-names></name><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>Bertola</surname><given-names>DR</given-names></name><name><surname>De Castro</surname><given-names>CI</given-names></name><name><surname>Koiffmann</surname><given-names>CP</given-names></name></person-group>:<article-title>A new case of interstitial 6q16.2 deletion in a patient with Prader-Willi-like phenotype and investigation of SIM1 gene deletion 